{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "SzqxY",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Onboarding",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "JlR5L",
          "name": "BriefTitle",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "Onboarding — brief",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "VmXOS",
          "name": "BriefBody",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "PURPOSE\nFirst boot of a self-hosted, single-user instance: create the one account, connect data sources, pick assets, offer a second factor, launch the first sync, and hand over to the app.\n\nENTRY POINTS\nAny request while no user exists → /setup (layout auth). The account lands on /onboarding/integrations, and the wizard (layout onboarding, no navigation) runs integraciones → activos → seguridad → listo → /welcome. Every other route sends a not-yet-onboarded reader back to step 1, which is why /welcome also uses the onboarding layout (D121).\n\nSCREENS (LEFT → RIGHT)\nMobile: Setup · Default, Setup · Error, Integrations, Assets, Seguridad, Complete, Welcome.\nDesktop: Setup (the auth split card: brand panel + form) and Welcome (the guide's three cards side by side). The wizard steps have no lg: layout — a centred max-w-2xl column — so they draw no desktop artboard (D4).\n\nBUSINESS RULES\n• Setup carries no Stepper: it creates the account; the four numbered steps start after it (OnboardingController::STEPS = 4).\n• Integrations lists every provider, keyed ones first in alphabetical order, each with what is lost without its key (ProviderDirectory#without). Keyless sources sit in their own box.\n• Assets preselects DEFAULT_SELECTED; the highlight follows the checkbox. Omitir goes to Seguridad, never past it.\n• Seguridad OFFERS enrolment and lets the reader skip (D52). Enrolment itself is auth.pen's TOTP screens.\n• Complete counts keys against the providers that take one.\n• Welcome is the only writer of onboarded_at (D30). Each guide card finishes onboarding and lands on its destination; the CTA lands on Panorama (D121).\n\nCOPY SOURCE\nconfig/locales/es-MX.yml — setup.new, onboarding.*, welcome.show, shared.welcome_body. Provider text: MarketData::Domain::ProviderDirectory and ProviderDefaults (provider_type). Asset rows: Administration::Domain::AssetCatalog. Setup errors: CreateFirstAdmin's contract, humanized field + message.\n\nSTATES NOT DRAWN\n• Integrations after setup: toast \"Cuenta creada. Ahora configura tu instancia.\"\n• Assets after saving keys: toast \"Llaves guardadas. Banxico respondió con %{count} tipo(s) de cambio.\" or \"Guardamos tus llaves, pero Banxico no respondió el tipo de cambio. Revisa el token en Integraciones.\"\n• Assets: the ACCIONES · MÉXICO group the catalog renders between ETFS and RENTA FIJA — held back while [ONB-5] is blocked.\n• Complete · Desktop, Seguridad · Desktop, Integrations · Desktop, Assets · Desktop: the same column, wider.\n• /help (D92): Welcome with title \"Ayuda y soporte\", its own subtitle, plain links, no CTA.\n\nOPEN FINDINGS\nNone with a D number. Board drafts: provider_type in English; CoinGecko recorded as keyless; contract errors in English; icon size classes; wordmark font.\n\nHISTORY\n→ Log · Onboarding",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
