          "id": "C8gNT",
          "name": "Entries",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "2026-09-16 · re-vendored to kit 1.0.0; ButtonPrimary, Field and Stepper back to the masters\n2026-09-16 · mirrored to the code (D78): Setup in the auth card, Integrations with all eight keyed providers, Assets with the full catalog, Seguridad as one card, Complete and Welcome resized; the brand-panel checklist retired with the artboard it lived on\n2026-09-16 · Setup · Error drawn; Integrations and Assets desktops retired (D4)\n2026-09-16 · D121 · Welcome leaves the app shell and its doors finish onboarding; with it, Complete reads step 4, Omitir stops skipping Seguridad, the key count drops keyless sources, and a failed setup keeps name and email\n2026-09-16 · canvas on the grid; the brief rewritten into its fixed sections\n2026-09-05 · D92 · /help stays undrawn on purpose — it is Welcome minus the CTA, so it earns a brief note rather than a 95% copy\n2026-09-05 · D91 · the Welcome body's bug link now opens the issue tracker; /report-bug was retired as hosted-beta residue\n2026-09-05 · this file adopted the Log frame, and the brief lost its three dated lines to it\n2026-08-27 · D52 · the wizard gained a fourth step, Seguridad; the Stepper went 3 → 4 across all five instances\n2026-08-27 · VOO and CETES split into their own cards — the code had already made the call, the brief was carrying it as an open question\n2026-08-27 · 🐞 fixed — the Welcome ContextCard's Mark was 56×56 inside a 28×28 Glyph, twice its frame and spilling out. The file's one reported layout problem",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
